[2026-03-14T23:29:52.551Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzG6wWH2YjG1dKJtcbYbog","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# netlify-env\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Sets environment variables on a Netlify site. The Netlify CLI (`npx netlify env:set`) frequently\n     6→fails with \"No project id found\" errors in monorepo and CI environments. Use the Netlify REST API\n     7→instead.\n     8→\n     9→## Usage\n    10→\n    11→Use `curl` to call the Netlify API directly. This is more reliable than the CLI.\n    12→\n    13→### Set an environment variable\n    14→\n    15→```bash\n    16→curl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    17→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    18→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    19→  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n    20→```\n    21→\n    22→### Update an existing environment variable\n    23→\n    24→```bash\n    25→curl -s -X PATCH \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    26→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    27→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    28→  -d '{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}'\n    29→```\n    30→\n    31→## Required Environment Variables\n    32→\n    33→- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`: API authentication token.\n    34→- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG`: The Netlify account slug (used in the API path).\n    35→- `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`: The site to set the variable on (passed as query parameter).\n    36→\n    37→### Verify an environment variable\n    38→\n    39→```bash\n    40→curl -s \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    41→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\"\n    42→```\n    43→\n    44→### Canonical workflow\n    45→\n    46→1. Read the value from `.env` (or `deployment.txt`).\n    47→2. Set via `curl -X POST` (for new variables) or `curl -X PATCH` (for existing ones).\n    48→3. Verify via `curl -X GET` to confirm the value was set correctly.\n    49→\n    50→Always use POST for initial creation. Using PATCH on a non-existent variable returns an error.\n    51→\n    52→## Notes\n    53→\n    54→- Do NOT use `npx netlify env:set` or `npx netlify env:get` — these commands fail in contexts\n    55→  where the CLI cannot resolve the project ID (monorepos, missing `.netlify/state.json`).\n    56→- The POST endpoint creates a new variable. If the variable already exists, use PATCH to update it.\n    57→- The `context` field controls which deploy contexts see the variable. Use `\"all\"` for production\n    58→  and preview deploys.\n    59→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b89a6be-cb49-4800-ac2f-ddeccb4462b9","uuid":"e633d8cc-ba29-494e-9212-e9e7d543437d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-env.md","content":"# netlify-env\n\n## Purpose\n\nSets environment variables on a Netlify site. The Netlify CLI (`npx netlify env:set`) frequently\nfails with \"No project id found\" errors in monorepo and CI environments. Use the Netlify REST API\ninstead.\n\n## Usage\n\nUse `curl` to call the Netlify API directly. This is more reliable than the CLI.\n\n### Set an environment variable\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n```\n\n### Update an existing environment variable\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X PATCH \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}'\n```\n\n## Required Environment Variables\n\n- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`: API authentication token.\n- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG`: The Netlify account slug (used in the API path).\n- `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`: The site to set the variable on (passed as query parameter).\n\n### Verify an environment variable\n\n```bash\ncurl -s \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\"\n```\n\n### Canonical workflow\n\n1. Read the value from `.env` (or `deployment.txt`).\n2. Set via `curl -X POST` (for new variables) or `curl -X PATCH` (for existing ones).\n3. Verify via `curl -X GET` to confirm the value was set correctly.\n\nAlways use POST for initial creation. Using PATCH on a non-existent variable returns an error.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Do NOT use `npx netlify env:set` or `npx netlify env:get` — these commands fail in contexts\n  where the CLI cannot resolve the project ID (monorepos, missing `.netlify/state.json`).\n- The POST endpoint creates a new variable. If the variable already exists, use PATCH to update it.\n- The `context` field controls which deploy contexts see the variable. Use `\"all\"` for production\n  and preview deploys.\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
