[2026-03-14T23:38:23.824Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014pgUoPz7wJ4hTmx52gvutq","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied. The only file that needed fixing was `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/notifications.ts`. It was using `pathParts[2]` and `pathParts[3]` to extract the notification ID and action, which would incorrectly grab the function name in production. Now it uses `pathParts.indexOf('notifications')` to find the function name's position and extracts the ID and action relative to that, matching the pattern already used in `teams.ts`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab59c9297cc725f2f (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 10798\ntool_uses: 6\nduration_ms: 24724</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b89a6be-cb49-4800-ac2f-ddeccb4462b9","uuid":"1c16f25e-5981-4b13-85ab-478ebe45cfaf","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/, several Netlify functions parse URL path parts incorrectly. \n\nThe problem: Functions use `pathParts[2]` or similar hardcoded indices to extract resource IDs from the URL. But in Netlify's production environment, the URL path is `/.netlify/functions/<function-name>/<resourceId>`, so `pathParts` after split('/').filter(Boolean) becomes `[\".netlify\", \"functions\", \"<function-name>\", \"<resourceId>\"]`. This means `pathParts[2]` returns the function name itself instead of the resource ID.\n\nThe fix: Instead of using hardcoded indices, find the function name in the path and get the next element. For example, in `notifications.ts`:\n```\nconst funcIndex = pathParts.indexOf('notifications');\nconst notificationId = funcIndex >= 0 ? pathParts[funcIndex + 1] || null : null;\nconst action = funcIndex >= 0 ? pathParts[funcIndex + 2] || null : null;\n```\n\nNote: The `teams.ts` file has already been fixed (uses `pathParts.indexOf('teams')`). Do NOT modify teams.ts.\n\nSearch ALL .ts files in /repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/ for pathParts usage and fix every instance. Only fix files that actually use pathParts with hardcoded indices to extract resource IDs.\n\nAlso, while you're in each file, if you see `details: String(err)` in any error response, that was a debug addition - leave it as is if present (only teams.ts has it).","agentId":"ab59c9297cc725f2f","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied. The only file that needed fixing was `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/notifications.ts`. It was using `pathParts[2]` and `pathParts[3]` to extract the notification ID and action, which would incorrectly grab the function name in production. Now it uses `pathParts.indexOf('notifications')` to find the function name's position and extracts the ID and action relative to that, matching the pattern already used in `teams.ts`."}],"totalDurationMs":24724,"totalTokens":10798,"totalToolUseCount":6,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":10202,"output_tokens":115,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":480},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
