[2026-03-14T23:39:50.601Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014CH5pfjrJZx4XCewTKRQ95","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Tools Overview\n\n## Purpose\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings from replay.io, allowing you to \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Investigation Methodology\nThe framework recommends: frame your question, use exploratory tools to identify related events, apply explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses supported by data, and document conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Exploratory Tools (Discovery)\n\n**Error Detection:**\n- UncaughtException and ReactException identification\n\n**Timeline Analysis:**\n- Timeline (combined events)\n- ConsoleMessages, LocalStorage, NetworkRequest\n- ReactRenders tracking\n\n**Source Code Investigation:**\n- ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources\n- Hit counts show execution frequency per line\n\n## Explanatory Tools (Understanding)\n\n**Dependency Tracking:**\n- GetStack (frame inspection)\n- ControlDependency (event causation chains)\n\n**State Details:**\n- DescribePoint and InspectElement\n- ReactComponents (component tree visualization)\n- Logpoint (expression value tracking across execution)\n- Evaluate (point-specific expressions)\n\n## Key Recommendation\n\"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful\" for tracking expression values throughout execution, identifying anomalies, and pursuing deeper investigation paths."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b89a6be-cb49-4800-ac2f-ddeccb4462b9","uuid":"09bf65e8-aeaa-4b56-ae1b-9a85da60577c","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Tools Overview\n\n## Purpose\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings from replay.io, allowing you to \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Investigation Methodology\nThe framework recommends: frame your question, use exploratory tools to identify related events, apply explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses supported by data, and document conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Exploratory Tools (Discovery)\n\n**Error Detection:**\n- UncaughtException and ReactException identification\n\n**Timeline Analysis:**\n- Timeline (combined events)\n- ConsoleMessages, LocalStorage, NetworkRequest\n- ReactRenders tracking\n\n**Source Code Investigation:**\n- ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources\n- Hit counts show execution frequency per line\n\n## Explanatory Tools (Understanding)\n\n**Dependency Tracking:**\n- GetStack (frame inspection)\n- ControlDependency (event causation chains)\n\n**State Details:**\n- DescribePoint and InspectElement\n- ReactComponents (component tree visualization)\n- Logpoint (expression value tracking across execution)\n- Evaluate (point-specific expressions)\n\n## Key Recommendation\n\"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful\" for tracking expression values throughout execution, identifying anomalies, and pursuing deeper investigation paths.","durationMs":3263,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T23:39:50.826Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WYYVqRFpto6HQm6KKVKDJZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay-Playwright Setup Guide\n\n## Installation Steps\n\nThe initial setup requires two components:\n\n1. **Plugin installation** via your package manager:\n   - `npm install --save-dev @replayio/playwright`\n   - Alternatives: yarn, pnpm, or bun with equivalent syntax\n\n2. **Browser installation**:\n   - `npx replayio install`\n\n## Authentication\n\nYou'll need to \"Create a Test Suite Team at https://app.replay.io/team/new/tests to generate an API key.\" Store it as an environment variable using `.env` file (recommended), or shell export commands.\n\n## Configuration\n\nYour `playwright.config.ts` needs these modifications:\n\n```typescript\nimport { replayReporter, devices as replayDevices } from \"@replayio/playwright\";\n\nconst config: PlaywrightTestConfig = {\n  reporter: [\n    replayReporter({\n      apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY,\n      upload: true,\n    }),\n    [\"line\"],\n  ],\n  projects: [\n    {\n      name: \"replay-chromium\",\n      use: { ...replayDevices[\"Replay Chromium\"] },\n    },\n  ],\n};\n```\n\nKey points: \"Preserve existing projects and reporters — add the Replay project alongside them.\" The `upload: true` setting enables automatic recording uploads.\n\n## Running Tests\n\nExecute tests using the Replay Browser with:\n```sh\nnpx playwright test --project replay-chromium\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nIf recordings aren't created despite successful test runs, the \"recording driver likely failed to load.\" Check for OpenSSL 1.1 compatibility issues on systems running OpenSSL 3, and set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` accordingly before launching the browser."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b89a6be-cb49-4800-ac2f-ddeccb4462b9","uuid":"ea6f2560-c29e-4a12-9161-124b43ea6a11","tool_use_result":{"bytes":5167,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay-Playwright Setup Guide\n\n## Installation Steps\n\nThe initial setup requires two components:\n\n1. **Plugin installation** via your package manager:\n   - `npm install --save-dev @replayio/playwright`\n   - Alternatives: yarn, pnpm, or bun with equivalent syntax\n\n2. **Browser installation**:\n   - `npx replayio install`\n\n## Authentication\n\nYou'll need to \"Create a Test Suite Team at https://app.replay.io/team/new/tests to generate an API key.\" Store it as an environment variable using `.env` file (recommended), or shell export commands.\n\n## Configuration\n\nYour `playwright.config.ts` needs these modifications:\n\n```typescript\nimport { replayReporter, devices as replayDevices } from \"@replayio/playwright\";\n\nconst config: PlaywrightTestConfig = {\n  reporter: [\n    replayReporter({\n      apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY,\n      upload: true,\n    }),\n    [\"line\"],\n  ],\n  projects: [\n    {\n      name: \"replay-chromium\",\n      use: { ...replayDevices[\"Replay Chromium\"] },\n    },\n  ],\n};\n```\n\nKey points: \"Preserve existing projects and reporters — add the Replay project alongside them.\" The `upload: true` setting enables automatic recording uploads.\n\n## Running Tests\n\nExecute tests using the Replay Browser with:\n```sh\nnpx playwright test --project replay-chromium\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nIf recordings aren't created despite successful test runs, the \"recording driver likely failed to load.\" Check for OpenSSL 1.1 compatibility issues on systems running OpenSSL 3, and set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` accordingly before launching the browser.","durationMs":4445,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-playwright/SKILL.md"}}
